{"adyghe": "ЦIыфхэр зэкIэри шъхьэфитхэу, ялъытэныгъэхэмджи, яфэшъуашъэхэмджи, зэфэдэхэу къэхъух.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "All human beings are born free and equal in dignity and rights", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-162", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 162}
{"adyghe": "Ахэмэ, акъылрэ, цIыфыгъэрэ, ахэлъышъ, - зэкъошныгъэ шапхъэм тетхэу цIыэнхэ фай.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "They are endowed with reason and conscience and should act towards one another in a spirit of brotherhood.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-163", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 163}
{"adyghe": "Жьыбгъэмрэ тыгъэмрэ зэнэкъокъух, Шъхьадж нахъ кIуачIэм фэдэу еIо зэкIоу къакIотгъэр алъэгъугъ ЦIыер щыгъэу.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "The breeze and the sun were arguing, each asserting that he was the strongest, when they saw a traveler who was advancing, wrapped in his coat.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-164", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 164}
{"adyghe": "Апэ цIыер зыщезгъэхрэр, Анахь кIуачIэу зэзэгъыгъэх.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "They agreed that whoever was the first to get the traveler to take off his coat would be regarded as the strongest.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-165", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 165}
{"adyghe": "Жьыбгъэр боу лъэщэу ащ епщагъ, ау, нахъ лъэщэу епщэфэ - зэкIом нахъ зыIчIеуцуахьы. Джаш пай уцуэжьыгъ.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "Then, the wind began to blow with all its force but the more it blew, the more the traveler tightened his coat around him and in the end, the wind gave up making him take it off.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-166", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 166}
{"adyghe": "ЕтIанэ тыгъэр къэщыугъ, зэкIор фабэ къапи цIыер зыщищхыыгъ. Ыджы, Жьыбгъэм, тыгъэр зэрэнахькIуачIэр къыгурыIуагъ.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "Then the sun started to shine and after a while, the traveler, warmed up, took off his coat. So the north wind had to recognize that the sun was the stronger of the two.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-167", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 167}
{"adyghe": "БэшIэгъэдэдэу къолэжъ горэ цIылагъ Ар псы ешъонэу фэягъ. Оджэ-моджэ къыблъабэхэу, псы лъыхъутыгъ. ЕтIанэ къошын горэ ылъэгъугъ.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "Once upon a time, there was a crow. He was thirsty. He was flying here and there in search of water. He wanted to drink water, but he could not find any. Then, he saw a pitcher.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-168", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 168}
{"adyghe": "Къошыным нахъ благъэу екIолIагъ. МакIэ ащ псэу итыгъэр, ыпэ нэсытэп. Ау боу Iушыгъ а къолэжъыр. Мыжъо цIыкIу заулэ къошынымди цIылъэу ылъэгъугъ.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "He moved closer to it. The level of water was very low in it. His beak could not reach the water, but the crow was very wise. He saw some little stones near the pitcher.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-169", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 169}
{"adyghe": "Мыжъо цIыкIухэр къыштэхи, псым хидзагъ. Псыр къыздэкIуатем ыпэ къынэси, ешъуи быбыжьыгъ.", "category": "parallel_text", "correction": null, "gloss_or_romanization": "He picked up those stones and dropped them in the water. Then the level of water increased. His beak reached the water, and he drank the water and flew away.", "id": "user-authored-adyghe-v0.1-170", "provenance": "user-authored", "source_line": 170}
